            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0199" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg149"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby, chargé, to
                        Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received August 16, 1894.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1872.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 1868, of the
                    18th instant, concerning the dispute in the island of Hainan over the choice of
                    a mission site, I have the honor to report that the viceroy has consented to the
                    selection of such a site in cooperation with the missionaries.</p>
                <p>I have expressed to the U. S. consul at Canton a hope that this consent will be
                    availed of to bring this dispute to a termination.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. Denby, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
